{"type":"assistant/message","seq":17,"time":1787561735892,"data":{"turn":1,"step":1,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"The user wants me to clean up their C drive. This is a Windows system task. Let me think about what this involves:\n\n1. First, I need to understand the current state of the C drive - how much space is used, what's taking up space\n2. Then identify safe cleanup targets (temp files, recycle bin, Windows Update cache, browser caches, etc.)\n3. Perform the cleanup\n\nThis is a potentially destructive operation, so I should be careful. Let me first check the current state of the C drive.\n\nMy working directory is D:\\windoc\\desktop\\3, but the C drive is the target. The sandbox policy is workspace-write, which means I can modify files under the session workspace D:\\windoc\\desktop\\3. Operations on C:\\ might be denied by the sandbox... Let me try to check.\n\nActually, let me start by checking the disk space situation on C:. This is a read-only operation that should be fine.\n\nLet me plan:\n1. Check C: drive free space and what's using space\n2. Identify cleanup candidates: temp files, recycle bin, Windows Update cache, hibernation file, browser caches, etc.\n3. Ask user for confirmation before deleting things (approval policy is \"ask\")\n\nLet me start with a disk overview. I'll use PowerShell commands.\n\nFirst, let me check the drive space."},{"type":"text","text":"我来帮你清理 C 盘。首先了解一下当前 C 盘的空间状况，再找出可以安全清理的内容。"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_PW9joyZpRchfyYyaobhK4944","name":"pwsh","arguments":"{\"command\": \"Get-PSDrive -PSProvider FileSystem | Select-Object Name, @{N='UsedGB';E={[math]::Round($_.Used/1GB,1)}}, @{N='FreeGB';E={[math]::Round($_.Free/1GB,1)}} | Format-Table -AutoSize\", \"description\": \"Show disk space usage for all drives\"}"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_sYXfnkpXkIWhrvOQbQoD7580","name":"pwsh","arguments":"{\"command\": \"$env:SystemDrive; $env:TEMP; $env:TMP; $env:LOCALAPPDATA; $env:A