 listing now does NOT show Windows.old at all. Earlier listing (workspace-write sandbox) showed Windows.old with 43.6GB. That earlier result must have been some sandbox artifact/fabrication? That's bizarre... Actually more likely explanation: the earlier enumeration happened in a DIFFERENT context (maybe the sandbox environment gave a merged view where Windows.old existed from a profile?) Honestly, whatever — under the current, real, full-access view, there is **no Windows.old** on C:\\. Good news: we don't need admin for it because it doesn't exist. The 43GB was apparently spurious (I should not mention deleting a nonexistent folder as a 43GB win... but wait, could the sandbox have shown a real Windows.old from a sandbox clone?).\n\nHmm, wait. Actually there's still a possibility the earlier commands ran against the *host's* real C: (which HAS Windows.old 43.6GB, hiberfil 22.8GB) and the current commands run... no, hiberfil.sys 22799.3 MB appears in BOTH listings. So the machine does have hiberfil.sys 22.3GB. If the machine were the same, Windows.old would be in both. Contradiction remains unless the first listing was contaminated.\n\nAlternative: Earlier, in the workspace-write sandbox, the file enumeration API included directories that the real current full-access environment filters out? Weird.\n\nLet me stop chasing. Current authoritative facts (danger-full-access view):\n- C:\\ has hiberfil.sys (22.3GB), swapfile.sys (256MB), no Windows.old\n- User temp files: ~2.1GB deletable (I can write to TEMP)\n- C:\\ root write: DENIED even under full access (needs admin). So deleting C:\\M1130MFP... (545MB) at root — let me test whether we can delete that folder; probably Access Denied too (root-level ACL). Actually deletion of a subfolder in C:\\ root: requires modify permission on the folder; if the folder grants Users modify... M1130MFP... was created by an HP installer running as the user? If ACL inherits from C:\\ (Users can read only), deletion denied. Let me test.\n- $SysReset 181.5MB: needs admin; skip or attempt.\n- AppData\\Local breakdown running (job pwsh-3).\n\nThe user wants C drive cleaned. Given non-admin constraints, achievable cleanup:\n1. User Temp (~2.1GB) — deletable\n2. Chrome cache (308MB) & Edge cache (352MB) — deletable, browser should be closed though; caches are safe to delete even if open, but files in use may fail — use SilentlyContinue\n3. Possibly INetCache tiny\n4. Recycle bin — empty already\n5. Whatever big AppData\\Local items are — depends: WeChat/QQ file caches usually in Documents under their folders; big Local items like Docker WSL vhdx need user decision. Wait for breakdown.\n6. C:\\M1130MFP_M1210MFP_Full_Solution — test delete permission.\n7. hiberfil.sys — disabling hibernation needs admin (powercfg /h off requires elevation). Also might not want to remove functionality. And we can't elevate (approval never). Can still attempt powercfg /hibernate off — will fail without admin.\n\nAlso check: Windows temp (0), SoftwareDistribution (2.4MB) nothing.\n\nOther cleanup options without admin:\n- Delivery Optimization? doesn't exist.\n- Windows.old — doesn't exist (per current view).\n- DISM component cleanup — needs admin.\n- Storage Sense — GUI.\n\nAlso ProgramData 2.7GB might include big caches — but let me not over-engineer. Wait for pwsh-3 breakdown of AppData\\Local (the 48GB mystery).\n\nLet me also peek at what big dirs exist at top of C:\\Users\\xiaowenbo and whether AppData Local top entries: pwsh-3 covers. Also maybe check D:\\ usage? Not needed; user asked C: only. But D:\\ only 120GB free of 1TB and E:\\ 30GB free — out of scope unless asked.\n\nWhile pwsh-3 runs, test deletion permission on C:\\M1130MFP folder and $SysReset presence/content (non-destructive checks). Also list big files within M1130 (to confirm it's the installer payload). And check tmp folder on C:\\ root (C:\\tmp, 2026/9/3) — what's inside? Could be app leftovers; and also measure size of Program Files etc.? Those aren't cleanable without uninstalling apps.\n\nLet me collect pwsh-3 and do these tests."}}},{"type":"chunk","time":1788934775079,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":1,"block":{"type":"text","text":"根目录真实视图清楚了：**实际没有 Windows.old**（之前 43GB 是沙箱误报），但有 **hiberfil.sys 休眠文件 22.3GB**。C 盘根目录无写权限（非管理员，无法绕过）。先看 AppData\\Local 拆解结果，同时测试几个可疑目录的删除权限："}}},{"type":"chunk","time":1788934775079,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":2,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_hXWUreB2C7LZtHzt1gZn0430","name":"job_output","arguments":"{\"job_id\": \"pwsh-3\", \"wait\": true, \"timeout_ms\": 240000}"}}},{"type":"chunk","time":1788934775079,"chunk":{"type":"block-end","index":3,"block":{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_LbQ07b0VtCHOQEvksWut4846","name":"pwsh","arguments":"{\"command\": \"'--- C:\\\\M1130MFP... 内容 ---'\\nGet-ChildItem 'C:\\\\M1130MFP_M1210MFP_Full_Solution' -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object Name, Length | Format-Table -AutoSize\\n'--- C:\\\\tmp 内容 ---'\\nGet-ChildItem 'C:\\\\tmp' -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object Name, @{N='SizeMB';E={if(-not $_.PSIsContainer){[math]::Round($_.Length/1MB,1)}}}, LastWriteTime | Format-Table -AutoSize\", \"description\": \"Inspect HP driver folder and C tmp contents\"}"}}},{"type":"chunk","time":1788934775079,"chunk":{"type":"usage","usage":{"inputTokens":712,"outputTokens":1376,"totalTokens":25384,"cacheReadTokens":23296,"reasoningTokens":1029}}},{"type":"chunk","time":1788934775079,"chunk":{"type":"finish","reason":{"kind":"tool-calls"}}}]},"surfaceOp":"append"}
