{"type":"assistant/message","seq":120,"time":1788934873792,"data":{"turn":2,"step":8,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","text":"Confirmed:\n- Yarn\\Cache is the Yarn v1 package cache (regenerable). bin empty, Data exists (Yarn Data probably global state—small). Delete contents of Yarn\\Cache → ~14GB.\n- pip\\cache → pip HTTP cache (regenerable). ~4.3GB.\n- npm-cache\\_cacache → npm cache (regenerable). ~1.9GB.\n- CrashDumps → crash dump files, safe to delete. 121MB.\n- HP printer M1210 MFP installed (matching M1130MFP_M1210MFP folder). The C:\\M1130MFP_M1210MFP_Full_Solution is the installer leftover for the installed printer. Safe to delete — but requires ACL at C:\\ root. Test it.\n- Hibernate is enabled and fast startup used. hiberfil.sys 22.3GB. Turning off hibernation needs admin — can't. And it would disable 快速启动 (fast startup) which the user's system uses; actually hiberfil being 22.8GB ≈ full RAM suggests full hibernation, not reduced. Since we can't run elevated anyway, I'll recommend the user do it manually with a command if they don't need hibernation. Actually hibernation and fast startup both rely on hiberfil. Removing = -22.3GB but slower boot + no hibernate. Offer instructions.\n\nRecycle bin showed 0 MB. Skip.\n\nNow cleanup plan (execute now):\n1. %TEMP% (user): delete contents except files in use. 2.1GB\n2. AppData\\Local\\Yarn\\Cache contents: ~14GB\n3. AppData\\Local\\pip\\cache: ~4.3GB\n4. AppData\\Local\\npm-cache\\_cacache + _npx? npm cache clean --force is cleaner; but direct deletion of _cacache is okay. Use npm cache clean? npm may not be on PATH in this session (PATH differs). Safer to delete directories directly with Remove-Item -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue. npm handles absence fine.\n5. CrashDumps: 121MB\n6. Chrome cache dir contents, Edge cache dir contents: ~660MB total (also these may be locked if browsers running — check running processes first; deletion will just fail on locked files, acceptable but browsers might recreate. Use SilentlyContinue.)\n7. C:\\M1130MFP_M1210MFP_Full_Solution: try delete (545MB) — attempt; skip on Access Denied and report.\n8. ProgramData? skip.\n9. JetBrains: only clear known-safe cache subfolders? Not worth risk; skip and explain.\n10. Re-run free space measurement and produce summary report.\n\nCareful: deleting yarn cache could be large count of files (tens of thousands). Remove-Item -Recurse can be slow. Better use cmd rd /s /q for speed? cmd /c rd works. But avoid capturing piped output (sandbox EPERM on piped stdio). pwsh Remove-Item is fine but slower; 14GB with many small files could take minutes. Use run_in_background with generous time, or use [System.IO.Directory]::Delete with recursive - faster but needs full language (we have). Under danger-full-access FullLanguage is available. Use Directory.Delete(path,true) in try/catch per target for speed and robustness, wrapping each so a failure doesn't abort the whole.\n\nPlan execution in a single background script that:\n- records before/after C: free (DriveInfo)\n- deletes each target, catches errors per target, writes a log line per target\n- returns summary output\n\nGiven many small files, per-target deletion may take a while; background with polling. Let me write it carefully to run in background. I'll create a .ps1? Simpler inline.\n\nBrowsers running check: Get-Process chrome,msedge → if running, deleting cache partially fails but that's fine; I could also skip. I'll just delete and report leftover.\n\nAlso add Windows Temp (C:\\Windows\\Temp 0MB anyway; deleting needs admin for some files; but only 0MB → skip).\n\nEmpty the user recycle bin too? 0MB. Skip.\n\nAdditionally: 待机 S3 supported etc. fine.\n\nLet me also handle one more thing — C:\\tmp\\codebuddy (folder inside C:\\tmp): what size? codebuddy might hold important things? C:\\tmp\\codebuddy LastWrite 2026/9/3. Might be Tencent CodeBuddy leftovers. Could check size but root ACL likely denies deletion anyway. Skip — but let me quickly measure & attempt as bonus only if ACL works (it won't). Fine.\n\nThen produce summary + optional admin steps.\n\nOne question worth asking user: none — do the safe stuff; report admin-needed list. JetBrains 9GB: might actually be largely cleanable cache (e.g., Toolbox downloads of IDE installers, plugin caches). But too risky to auto-nuke. I'll include a targeted list at the end with a suggested safe subset if they want more.\n\nHmm, wait: total deletable = 2.1+14+4.3+1.9+0.12+0.66+0.55 ≈ 23.6GB → C free would go from 49.4 to ~73GB. \n\nAlso consider: PowerShell running Remove-Item with -Recurse -Force on _cacache — npm uses content-addressable; deletion fine.\n\nFor Yarn\\Cache: contents are zip files under versioned subfolders (v6 etc). Delete all contents.\n\nEdge cache path: AppData\\Local\\Microsoft\\Edge\\User Data\\Default\\Cache (352MB). Chrome: ...\\Google\\Chrome\\User Data\\Default\\Cache (308MB). Plus Code Cache dirs maybe bigger (Google folder total 2.7GB incl profile). Deleting only the Cache subdirs keeps profiles.\n\nActually Google folder 2694MB total, Chrome Cache only 308MB measured... so Chrome profile includes more (Code Cache, GPUCache, Service Worker). But don't over-delete; Cache + Code Cache + GPUCache are safe (regenerated). Keep it modest: Cache folder only. Fine, 308MB.\n\nLet me estimate remaining free space precisely with DriveInfo before/after.\n\nWrite the cleanup command. I'll run in background and also monitor. Use single pwsh with try/catch per item, exit 0, output summary with per-item status and freed MB, plus before/after drive free.\n\nDeletion targets (paths):\nA. \"$env:LOCALAPPDATA\\Temp\" contents (not the folder itself)\nB. \"$env:LOCALAPPDATA\\Yarn\\Cache\" contents\nC. \"$env:LOCALAPPDATA\\pip\\cache\" (folder itself)\nD. \"$env:LOCALAPPDATA\\npm-cache\" — delete whole folder? npm recreates. Includes _cacache,_logs,_npx,_update-notifier. Deleting all fine (~1.9GB). Keep folder and delete contents to be safe with open handles; deleting contents works.\nE. \"$env:LOCALAPPDATA\\CrashDumps\" contents\nF. Chrome cache contents\nG. Edge cache contents\nH. C:\\M1130MFP_M1210MFP_Full_Solution (whole) — best-effort\n\nUse helper function Remove-Contents($p) or Remove-Tree. For contents-deletion: iterate Get-ChildItem and Directory.Delete/File.Delete with recursive. But simplest robust: cmd-style via [System.IO.Directory]::Delete for subdirs + files. I'll implement:\n\nfunction Clear-Folder($path){\n  if(-not (Test-Path -LiteralPath $path)){ return \"跳过(不存在): $path\" }\n  $items = Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $path -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue\n  $freed = (Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $path -Recurse -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Measure-Object Length -Sum).Sum\n  $ok=0;$fail=0\n  foreach($it in $items){\n    try{\n      if($it.PSIsContainer){ [System.IO.Directory]::Delete($it.FullName,$true) } else { [System.IO.File]::Delete($it.FullName) }\n      $ok++\n    }catch{ $fail++ }\n  }\n  \"完成: $path (删除 $ok 项, 失败 $fail 项, 约释放 $([math]::Round($freed/1MB)) MB)\"\n}\nFor whole folder C:\\M1130...: try Directory.Delete($path,$true).\n\nThen print before/after free GB via DriveInfo.\n\nRun in background, then check output. Also todo list to show progress."},{"type":"text","text":"内部结构确认，可以放心清理的都是**可再生缓存**。HP 打印机（M1210）已安装，C 盘根目录那个 545MB 是**安装包残留**，可删。现在执行清理："},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_00_ifzhEpUtplzoRQqIVJmw5010","name":"todo_write","arguments":"{\"todos\": [{\"content\": \"分析 C 盘空间占用\", \"status\": \"completed\"}, {\"content\": \"清理用户 Temp / CrashDumps\", \"status\": \"in_progress\"}, {\"content\": \"清理 Yarn / pip / npm 缓存\", \"status\": \"in_progress\"}, {\"content\": \"清理浏览器缓存\", \"status\": \"in_progress\"}, {\"content\": \"删除 HP 驱动安装包残留\", \"status\": \"pending\"}, {\"content\": \"验证释放空间并汇总报告\", \"status\": \"pending\"}]}"},{"type":"tool-call","id":"call_01_nzWPQhIiRmlkwDQexXF66496","name":"pwsh","arguments":"{\"command\": \"$before = ([System.